\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 README: Tsalagi Guess Who game May 2026
\f1\b0 \
\
Made by Jessie Tanner with help from Google Gemini.\
I got lots of help from Charlie McVicker who helped find an open source for illustrations by Pablo Stanley\
(https://openpeeps.com/).\
\

\f0\b Setup\

\f1\b0 You and your opponent should both have the .html file and the folder of images downloaded on your computer. Both of you should double click the .html file to launch the game. This will set up a private game board for each of you to use while you talk on another platform \'97 on the phone, Discord, Zoom, or across the table from one another.\
\

\f0\b How to Play
\f1\b0 \
First, each of you should choose a secret character to play as. The other person is trying to guess who you are, so don\'92t tell them. If you want, you can use the random button to choose someone; otherwise, make your own choice.\
\
Take turns asking each other questions. Any question is game if it is asked in Cherokee. I have given some possible questions at the bottom. I used JW Webster\'92s tone system and consulted with him on translations. This is not an exhaustive list of all the possible questions you could ask.\
\
Using the information you get from the other player, eliminate possible characters from contention by clicking on their picture to cross them out.\
\
